# Code owners — the humans whose review a pull request into main needs.
#
# Load-bearing for the nightly ledger PR: the org allows GitHub Actions to OPEN pull
# requests, and GitHub's single switch would let it approve them too. With this file
# in place, `require_code_owner_review` on main means only an owner's approval counts,
# so a bot's approval is inert by construction — Actions can propose, never ratify.
